atory substitutions restore normal core assembly in simian immunodeficiency virus isolates with Gag epitope cytotoxic T-lymphocyte escape mutations.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>8168</fpage><lpage>8177</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16873273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002422-Richman1"><label>47</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richman</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wrin</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Little</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Petropoulos</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Rapid evolution of the neutralizing antibody response to HIV type 1 infection.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>100</volume><fpage>4144</fpage><lpage>4149</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12644702</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002422-Jansen1"><label>48</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jansen</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kostense</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vandenberghe</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nanlohy</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>De Cuyper</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>High responsiveness of HLA-B57-restricted Gag-specific CD8&#x0002b; T cells in vitro may contribute to the protective effect of HLA-B57 in HIV-infection.</article-title><source>European Journal of Immunology</source><volume>35</volume><fpage>150</fpage><lpage>158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15593302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002422-Klein1"><label>49</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klein</